CAT = "bcgReports"; SEG = "REP"
Q = [
("Your report names a visitor who was badly hurt on site. Under PIPA, the company may disclose the visitor's information without consent to:",
 "Contact the visitor's next of kin", ["Inform the visitor's employer", "Notify the visitor's insurer", "Tell the visitor's landlord"],
 "Personal Information Protection Act s. 18(1)(l): an organization may disclose personal information without consent to contact next of kin or a friend of an injured, ill or deceased individual."),
("A good incident report records:",
 "Facts you observed", ["Facts and your conclusions", "What the client asks you to note", "A summary agreed with coworkers"],
 "A report is a factual record. Opinions and guesses can be challenged, and the Code of Conduct bars wilful or negligent false statements."),
("A company discloses a person's information without consent because of compelling health or safety circumstances. Under PIPA it must also:",
 "Mail notice to the person", ["Get the person's consent later", "Tell the registrar within 14 days", "Keep the request for a year"],
 "Personal Information Protection Act s. 18(1)(k): disclosure is allowed when compelling circumstances affect someone's health or safety, if notice of the disclosure is mailed to the last known address of the individual it is about."),
("A guard works alone and checks in with a dispatcher. Under WorkSafeBC rules, who must record the results of each check?",
 "The person who makes the checks", ["The lone guard, in the log", "The guard's supervisor only", "The employer's safety committee"],
 "WorkSafeBC OHS Regulation 4.21(3): a person must be designated to contact the lone worker at set intervals, and that person must record the results."),
("An employer must instruct guards who may face violence in how to:",
 "Report and document incidents", ["Restrain a violent person", "Disarm someone with a weapon", "Detain people who threaten staff"],
 "WorkSafeBC OHS Regulation 4.30(3)(d): workers at risk of violence must be instructed in the procedures for reporting, investigating and documenting incidents of violence."),
("A person asks your company to correct an incident report about them. If the company decides not to change it, under PIPA it must:",
 "Note the correction asked for", ["Correct it anyway", "Delete the disputed part", "Refer it to the commissioner"],
 "Personal Information Protection Act s. 24(3): if no correction is made, the organization must annotate the information with the correction that was requested but not made."),
("When a person makes a threat, record it:",
 "Word for word", ["Word for word, minus swearing", "Summarized in plain words", "In the speaker's general meaning"],
 "Exact words are evidence. A summary can change the meaning and is easier to challenge."),
("Physical evidence you find at a scene should be:",
 "Left in place for police", ["Photographed, then bagged by you", "Moved somewhere safe", "Handed to the client's manager"],
 "Leaving evidence undisturbed protects it. Moving or cleaning it can destroy what police need."),
("Writing that you saw something you only heard about from someone else is:",
 "A false statement", ["Fine if you name no one", "Acceptable if likely true", "Allowed if you sign it"],
 "The Code of Conduct bars wilful or negligent false statements. Write that a named person told you, and what they said."),
("A security business must keep a record of each worker's:",
 "Hours and duties per shift", ["Training school transcript", "Emergency contact person", "Uniform and kit issued"],
 "Section 7 of the regulation lists worker records such as name, address, licence number, payroll, hours worked and the type of work on each shift."),
("Who should write the report on an incident you handled?",
 "You, from your own notes", ["Your supervisor, from your notes", "You, from the client's CCTV", "You and a coworker together"],
 "The person who saw and handled the incident writes the report from their own notes. A second-hand account is weaker evidence."),
("Times in your notes should be recorded:",
 "Exactly as they occur", ["To the nearest quarter hour", "At the start and end of each event", "As shown on the client's clock"],
 "Exact times build a timeline that can be checked against video, alarms and other records."),
("Under PIPA, may your company give police an incident report to help them investigate an offence, without the person's consent?",
 "Yes, PIPA allows it", ["Only after telling the person", "Only with the person's consent", "Only if police get a warrant"],
 "Personal Information Protection Act s. 18(1)(j): an organization may disclose personal information without consent to a law enforcement agency in Canada to assist in an investigation of an offence."),
("You handcuff a shoplifter who does not resist at all. A use-of-force report is:",
 "Still required", ["Not needed for handcuffs alone", "Not needed if he agreed", "Needed only if he is hurt"],
 "Handcuffing is force, and Security Services Regulation s. 7(1)(g) and registrar policy 3.7.2 require a report for any type of force, including when a restraining device is used."),
("A licensed guard employed directly by a hotel, not by a security company, uses force on duty. Under registrar policy the guard:",
 "Must keep a use-of-force report", ["Reports it to the hotel's manager instead", "Needs no report, being in-house", "Keeps a report only if police attend"],
 "Registrar policy 3.7.2.1 makes keeping use-of-force reports a condition of every security worker licence, including workers employed by a non-security business."),
("Someone asks a security business to duplicate a restricted key. The business must record:",
 "The person's name and address", ["The key code and the date", "The person's photo ID number", "The owner's written consent"],
 "Security Services Regulation s. 7(1)(a): the records include the name and address of the person asking, and of the key's owner if that is someone else."),
("For each witness, your report should record:",
 "Full name and contact details", ["Full name and date of birth", "Full name and employer", "Full name and description"],
 "Police and investigators may need to reach a witness later. A first name alone is rarely enough."),
("Instead of writing \"the man was drunk\", a better report describes:",
 "What you observed", ["That he appeared drunk", "What the bartender believed", "Your best estimate of drinks"],
 "Observations such as slurred speech, unsteady walking and an odour of liquor are facts; \"drunk\" is a conclusion."),
("Under PIPA, a person asking a company for their own information, or for a correction, must make the request:",
 "In writing", ["By phone or in writing", "In person, with photo ID", "By email to the registrar"],
 "Personal Information Protection Act s. 27: a request for access or correction must be made in writing, with enough detail to identify the information."),
("A report that leaves out force you used during an incident is:",
 "Incomplete and misleading", ["Complete if force is on another form", "Acceptable if the force was minor", "Misleading only if someone was hurt"],
 "Licensees must record any use of force, and the Code bars negligent false statements. Leaving force out paints a false picture."),
]
